# Local logs and output (large/noisy, not needed in cloud)
dman_logs/
dman_pro_backtest.csv
dman_signals_*.json

# State files below are committed by GitHub Actions to persist between runs.
# DO NOT re-add them here — they must be tracked for cloud state continuity:
#   dman_win_rate.json          (WinRateTracker, adaptive score, consecutive loss guard)
#   dman_positions.json         (PositionTracker, MAX_POSITIONS, duplicate order guard)
#   dman_monthly_pnl.json       (monthly loss circuit breaker)
#   dman_alpaca_sync.json       (Alpaca fill sync — which fills already recorded)
#   dman_earnings_pending.json  (awaiting-approval earnings spreads)
#   dman_rate_limit_events.json (today's Alpaca 429 counts — watchdog reads this)

# Local Windows scheduled task wrappers (not needed in cloud)
dman_run.ps1
dman_eod.ps1

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The repo root is the HOME directory, so .vscode/ here holds the entire VS Code
# extension tree and CLI payload -- hundreds of MB. A stray `git add -A` would
# stage all of it. Ignore those, but KEEP settings.json tracked (see the
# negation): it carries the Pylance configuration this workspace needs, and on
# 2026-10-12 a bad analysis.exclude in it cost an hour of false errors.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# ── The repo root is the HOME directory ──────────────────────────────────
# Measured 2026-10-14: `git add -A` here would stage ~44 GB -- AppData alone
# is 38.6 GB, Downloads 3.9 GB, OneDrive 1.5 GB, .claude 535 MB. `git status`
# looks harmless (88 ms) only because git reports an untracked DIRECTORY
# without recursing into it; `git add` does recurse. The .vscode/* rule above
# was added for exactly this reason and the reasoning was never extended to
# the rest of the profile.
#
# Every pattern is ANCHORED with a leading slash so it matches only at the
# repo root. In the cloud checkout the root is the repo itself and none of
# these exist, so they are no-ops there -- an unanchored "Music/" could
# otherwise shadow a real subdirectory someday.
#
# Verified: none of the 76 tracked files is matched by any rule below.
/AppData/
/OneDrive/
/Downloads/
/Contacts/
/Favorites/
/Links/
/Music/
/Videos/
/Searches/
/Saved Games/
/BrawlhallaReplays/

# Windows registry hives, rewritten constantly while logged in
/NTUSER.DAT
/NTUSER.DAT{*
/ntuser.dat.LOG*
/ntuser.ini

# Per-tool local state that happens to live in the home directory
/.claude/
/.claude.json
/.claude.json.tmp.*
/.config/
/.copilot/
/.vscode-shared/
/.gitconfig

# Frozen harness inputs are local-only by design -- see backtest_harness.py:
# "The frozen data (golden/fixtures/backtest_bars.pkl) is local only"
/golden/fixtures/
